          "english_quote": "wishing to expose them as having gone still further astray",
          "issue": "The main rendering defensibly attaches ἐπὶ πλεῖον to their being astray, but the phrase can instead qualify ἐλέγξαι: wishing to demonstrate their error more fully. These readings distinguish greater error from a fuller demonstration of error. The existing note discusses the attachment of τοὺς προφήτας but does not disclose this separate scope ambiguity. This is an interpretive disclosure issue, not evidence of source corruption.",
          "suggested_revision": "Extend the note to preserve both scopes. For example: “The main rendering takes ἐπὶ πλεῖον with the following αὐτοὺς πεπλανημένους, expressing a greater degree of error. Alternatively, it can qualify ἐλέγξαι: ‘wishing to demonstrate more fully that they had gone astray.’ The position before the predicative phrase supports the chosen attachment, but does not exclude the alternative.” The main wording may remain as a disclosed contextual choice; the revised note requires fresh review.",
